      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ottawa Hills began its development in 1915, when the village was first laid out by planners and architects.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John North Willys, president of the Overland Company, bought about 1,200 acres at Bancroft and Indian Roads, stretching to the Ottawa River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nearly one‑third of Ottawa Hills—about 35%—has been set aside for parks and open space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The portion of the village next to Secor Road and south of Bancroft Street follows the original 1915 layout almost exactly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Many of Ottawa Hills’ oldest homes sit in Plat 1, where founder John North Willys himself once lived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
